# A master's floor: a will asks first, and takes only with the leave
#
# The smelter stands on the smith's protected floor with no charcoal rake, and the rake lies on the
# hearth. His will's nearest aim is to take it up. Without leave taking it is a theft, which a will that
# wants a grab does not plan, so the plan is the lawful one, two steps: ask the smith, grab the rake.
# `inspect workshops` reads the gates directly: the hearth, the one station his trade works, is offered
# only as a crime until the leave is given.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-mm smelting --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Forge" --period dawn

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

expect-state workshops usable=none
expect-state workshops crime=Test_Forge_Hearth
expect-state will will smelting steps=2
expect-state will for the use of the test smithy
expect-state will grab a charcoal rake
quit
